    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.sparse.to_dense — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.sparse.to_dense#\n\n- DataFrame.sparse.to_dense()[source]#\n- Convert a DataFrame with sparse values to dense. This method converts all SparseArray columns in the DataFrame to regular NumPy arrays. \n  - Returns:\n    - DataFrame\n    - A DataFrame with the same values stored as dense arrays.\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.sparse.density`\n  - Ratio of non-sparse points to total (dense) data points.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"A\": pd.arrays.SparseArray([0, 1, 0])}) >>> df.sparse.to_dense() A 0 0 1 1 2 0",
